  "ref": "ACT.23.15",
  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected the placement of of in judge of his case. The accepted alignment applied rule 106's accusative arm to the article τά and left περί unrepresented under rule 36's compression clause, but that clause reaches only a phrase the ASV renders with no preposition at all (τὰ περὶ ἡμῶν → our state); here a preposition is written. Rule 106 itself defers to rule 36 wherever a Greek preposition is expressed.",
    "The chapter reads an expressed preposition this way everywhere else: 23.11 τὰ περὶ ἐμοῦ → concerning me, 23.20 περὶ αὐτοῦ → concerning him, and 23.34 ἐκ ποίας ἐπαρχείας → asked of what province, where of goes to ἐκ though asked of reads phrasal. ACT.23.16 ἀκούσας τὴν ἐνέδραν → heard of remains the contrast, no preposition standing there.",
    "BSB reports this token as represented; the correction agrees with it, but rule 36 and rule 106 are what carry it and the reference comparison is only corroboration.",
    "Every other unit, head and note is as the verse pass returned it."
  ]
